course: dictionary
lesson: 6033
title: Melody: the tune
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A melody is a tune. It is a series of musical notes, one after another, that sounds pleasing and is easy to remember. Hum a song you know and you are humming its melody.
explain: The example says, «Many pop songs share the same four chords in the same order; songs differ in melody, words and sound.» The sentence lists melody next to words and sound as separate things. So melody must mean the tune itself, not the words.
explain: Words around the word give more clues. «A catchy melody» means a tune that sticks in your head. «Play the melody» means play the main tune. Ask yourself: is this about the notes that make the tune?
fact: A melody is a tune: notes played one after another that sound pleasing.
fact: The melody is often the main part of a piece of music, and it is often the part that is sung.
fact: Melody is different from rhythm, which is the beat pattern, and from harmony, which is notes played together.
fact: «A catchy melody» means a tune that is easy to remember.
fact: «Melody» can also mean any pleasant sound, such as birdsong.
exercise: «Songs differ in melody, words and sound.» In this sentence, what does melody mean? | The words that are sung | The name of the singer | The beat pattern of a drum | *The tune of a song, made of notes
exercise: Ruby says, «Hum the melody.» What does she want you to do? | Play the drums very fast | Stop the music | Shout the words loudly | *Sing or hum the tune without the words
exercise: Which of these best describes a melody? | A beat that keeps time | A loud crash | *A tune made of notes, one after another | Notes played together at the same moment
test: «A catchy melody» is a tune that is what? | Hard to hear | Only played on drums | Always sung in a whisper | *Easy to remember
test: In a story, «a sweet melody drifted through the air.» What is the melody here? | A heavy wooden box | A sharp cold wind | A path through the forest | *A pleasant sound, like music
exam: In music lessons, you learn melody, rhythm and harmony. Which one means notes played together? | Melody | Rhythm | *Harmony | Silence
